#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: sunless sea.
#> pause: 45
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> must: A stately pleasure dome decree:
#> must: Down to a sunless sea.
#> not: Where Alph
#> not: measureless
#> source: /Alph/,/caverns/d
# 7. Two addresses select a range. McMahon 2.3
# "addr1,addr2" applies the function from the first line matching addr1 up to
# and including the next line matching addr2, then starts looking for addr1
# again. /Alph/,/caverns/d therefore removes lines 3 and 4. A range may mix
# kinds: 2,/caverns/ or /Alph/,$ work too. One address: just the lines it hits.
# Try: make it /Alph/,/nowhere/d; an unmatched addr2 runs to the end of input.
/Alph/,/caverns/d

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
